diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index ebe2da3..5e195e0 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -39,7 +39,7 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **UI threading model.** `app.App` holds all state. The view (`App.View`) runs on the main thread every frame and only reads state. Network work runs on goroutines and writes results back through `a.update(fn)`, which is `Window.Update` in the real app. With no window (tests), it queues `fn` and `runQueued` drains the queue at the start of the next frame. Never mutate `App` state directly from a goroutine. Toasts and clipboard writes need a `*ui.Context`, so code outside the view queues them (`a.toast`, `a.pendingToasts`, `a.copy`) and the view flushes them.
 
-**Phases and routing.** `App.phase` is booting → login → ready. Once ready, `shell.go` draws the sidebar and title bar around a `ui.Router` with these routes: `/files/{path...}` (netdisk path, segments `url.PathEscape`d by `filesRoute`/`dirOfRoute`), `/search?q=`, `/transfers`, `/shares`, `/offline`, `/recycle`, `/settings`. The title bar's controls switch on `a.section()`. Each directory gets its own `listing` (cached in `a.listings`, keyed by dir), so a page sliding out during a router transition keeps showing its own files.
+**Phases and routing.** `App.phase` is booting → login → ready. Once ready, `shell.go` draws the sidebar and title bar around a `ui.Router` with these routes: `/files/{path...}` (netdisk path, segments `url.PathEscape`d by `filesRoute`/`dirOfRoute`), `/search?q=`, `/transfers`, `/shares`, `/offline`, `/dedup`, `/recycle`, `/settings`. The title bar's controls switch on `a.section()`. Each directory gets its own `listing` (cached in `a.listings`, keyed by dir), so a page sliding out during a router transition keeps showing its own files.
 
 **Overlays.** One `a.dlg` (`dialog` with a `dialogKind`) drives every modal through `a.dialogs`. The file preview is a separate overlay (`a.pv`, `previewOverlay`). The image preview and the grid/list thumbnails share `ui.ElementTransition{Match: thumbMatch{fsid}}`. The source thumbnail is skipped while `a.previewing(f)`, so the image grows out of it and shrinks back.
 
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ Dev-only environment variables (see `capture.go`, `app/app.go`, `app/session.go`
 
 **Fake netdisk (`internal/fakepan`).** An `httptest` server that emulates every web endpoint the client uses, over an in-memory tree with generated images, a PDF and a WAV. App UI tests (`app/*_test.go`, helper `signedIn` in `app/app_test.go`) drive real views with `ui.Tester` against it. When adding a new API call, add its endpoint to fakepan too.
 
+**Duplicate files (`internal/dedup`).** The dedup page reads no file content: `dedup.Scan` walks the folders under a root four at a time (capped at 50,000 files and 5,000 folders, cancelable, reporting progress), and `dedup.Groups` groups what it found by size and MD5, the hash the list API already returns (scrambled there, decrypted in `internal/baidu/list.go` with `baidupcs.DecryptMD5`). Entries with no MD5 are counted and skipped as `缺少哈希，已跳过`; 0-byte files and single files are no group. Groups come by the space freeing all but one copy would free. `app/dedup.go` runs the scan on a goroutine and writes back through `a.update`, throttling progress to about every 180 ms; it keeps the earliest modified copy of each group by default (its path breaking a tie), and `Client.Delete` moves the chosen copies to the recycle bin. The web `filemetas` endpoint is not used to fill in missing hashes.
+
 **No-disk previews.** `internal/remote` reads files into memory via Range requests (`ReadAll` with size limits, or a seekable `File` with a chunk cache for streaming audio) and re-requests the link on 403. PDFs render through `internal/pdf`: PDFium compiled to WebAssembly, run in wazero, pool started lazily by `pdf.Warm`. The PDF viewer lays its pages out itself in a `ScrollBoth` (`layoutPDF`), zooms like the image viewer (pinch, Cmd with the wheel, Cmd +/-/0, the buttons) keeping the point under the pointer on its page, and draws each page whole at 2 px per DIP up to `pdfPixels`; zoomed in further, the part in view (plus `pdfAround`) is drawn over it with `RenderPart`, snapped to the whole page's pixels so the two line up. Pages far from view drop their pictures. Video, and audio formats MyGo's `audio` package can't decode, go to mpv via `internal/player` with `--user-agent` and `--http-header-fields-append=Cookie: …`.
 
 **Transfers (`internal/transfer`).** `Manager` is a queue run by `Parallel`. Downloads fetch 4 MB blocks over `Threads` connections into `<file>.bngdl`, with a `.bngdl.json` sidecar of finished blocks for resume. Task state persists to `transfers.json` in the user data dir. `OnChange`/`OnFinish` are called outside the manager's lock and read tasks back through `Tasks()`. Don't call them while holding `m.mu`: that deadlocked once.
